# Review: EchoSqlite

The package matches its spec closely and is well tested. `SqliteDatabase` opens by migrating and
loading type rows only. It holds hydrated entities in a `WeakRef` working set with a
`FinalizationRegistry`, and writes dirty rows behind in one transaction per microtask, requeueing a
failed batch. `compileQuery` emits one `WITH RECURSIVE` statement of `CROSS JOIN`ed CTEs with
bound values, typed JSON comparisons, the FTS5 table, the reverse-reference table and the
depth-10 deletion cascade. Every feature group has named tests in `database.test.ts`,
`memory.test.ts`, `differential.test.ts`, `explain.test.ts` and `schema.test.ts`.

Three gaps. The entity table has only the normalized `parent_id`/`source_id`/`target_id`
columns, not the raw URI columns F-2.2 lists. An unknown type hydrates through `objectFromJSON` as an
ordinary live object, or the row is skipped on a decode error, rather than as a read-only snapshot
(F-7.3). T-1 seeds 2,000 objects, not 100,000, and its heap clause runs only in the manual
`memory.report.test.ts`. Browser and bun SqlClients (F-1.2) and the registry scope (F-4.10) have no
tests.

Of 47 items: 42 done, 2 untested, 3 partial, 0 diverged, 0 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

